cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Cited for the cryptoperiod framing (§5.3.6): signing keys that
  certify other keys are the highest-value keys in the system and thus have
  the tightest recommended cryptoperiod."
title: "Recommendation for Key Management: Part 1 — General"
type: standard
authors:
  - name: "Barker, Elaine"
identifiers:
  - type: other
    value: NIST SP 800-57 Part 1 Rev. 5
url: "https://csrc.nist.gov/publications/detail/sp/800-57-part-1/rev-5/final"
date-released: 2020-05
license: "US public domain (NIST)"
notes: "§5.3.6 tables the recommended cryptoperiods by key type. Public
  signature-verification keys used to certify other public keys carry the
  strongest expectation of a bounded originator usage period. RFD 2145's
  10-year table row for the root's notAfter and 5-year policy rotation sit
  well inside NIST's directional bound."
